            "URL": "https://salsa.debian.org/security-tracker-team/security-tracker"
          },
          "Title": "util-linux: util-linux: Partition metadata compromise via integer overflow in DOS partition parser",
          "Description": "util-linux is a random collection of Linux utilities. Before util-linux 2.41.4, `parse_dos_extended()` in `libblkid/src/partitions/dos.c` computes an extended-partition start sector with 32-bit addition and does not apply the extended-area bounds checks to the first two EBR entries. A local attacker who causes a crafted DOS extended-partition disk image or removable medium to be probed can wrap `cur_start + start` to sector zero and cause libblkid to report a false partition overlapping the MBR. This directly compromises the integrity of the reported partition metadata; disk modification or availability loss requires a separate downstream consumer to act on that metadata. This issue is fixed in 2.41.4.",
          "Severity": "HIGH",
          "CweIDs": [
            "CWE-190"
          ],
          "VendorSeverity": {
            "amazon": 3,
            "redhat": 3,
            "ubuntu": 2
          },
          "CVSS": {
            "redhat": {
              "V3Vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:H",
              "V3Score": 8
            }
          },
